From ac22b8698126eb50693fc52d8edfe6680a5bcf04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:23:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] Add the XD link fix: Emerald hook, XD shim and emulator
 test

XD sends its own GBA programs (trade and battle), which Emerald runs as
sent. A hook in Emerald's copyright-screen code (in place of its Colosseum
check, which it still does) recognises XD's programs by hash, makes their
loader jump to XdPostLoad after decompression, and that copies a shim to
the top of EWRAM and redirects IdentifyFlash, ReadFlash, VerifyFlashSector
(NBytes) and the link save step to it. The shim serves the save with the
Colosseum repro backend, unchanged.

analyze_xd.py finds everything per program (flash library by signature,
call sites, variables, memory use, that every write goes through the save
step); make_xd_tables.py turns that into addresses and hashes only.
xd_emu_test.py runs Emerald's patched code, XD's real loader and save code
against the simulated carts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014JPQshc9oBXnzvR2E67Khm
